@NebbioloNerd @OHare888 I'm not tracking how this is "embarrassing for the US". Iran got walloped and none of the naysayers' predictions came true ("there are going to be hundreds of troop deaths and massive destruction", "oil is going to $200 and the world economy is going to collapse")

No credible geopolitical analyst predicted the regime would fall without ground troops; it was an upside shot at best. There's little need to continue military operation because the objectives have been met and regime change would be too costly and risky to pursue

And $4mil interceptors vs. $250K missiles is just the physics of missile defense; it will always be that way. It's simply much easier to load a warhead with rocket fuel and a TEMU GPS than intercept one in terminal phase from a ground-based launcher where >95% success is needed.

